Lobium - navigator.* and User-Agent / UA client hints, natively.

Split out of core/config-channel.patch: transport and surfaces are separate concerns, and this is
the surface that touches the most upstream files.

All of these read lobium::LobiumFpConfig::Current() and fall back to the real host value when the
config is absent or the field is unset:

  * components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc - the HTTP User-Agent request header AND
    Sec-CH-UA metadata (GetUserAgent + GetUserAgentMetadata), browser-side. This is the deepest
    shared UA source, so navigations, subresources AND all three worker types send the persona UA
    and branded Sec-CH-UA - closing the worker-header leak a per-frame CDP override never reached,
    and removing the unbranded-Chromium tell natively.
  * third_party/blink/renderer/core/execution_context/navigator_base.cc - navigator.userAgent and
    navigator.platform in EVERY context, workers included.
  * third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_concurrent_hardware.cc - hardwareConcurrency.
  * third_party/blink/common/device_memory/approximated_device_memory.cc - deviceMemory, which is
    also the single source for the Device-Memory client hint, so the JS getter and the header agree
    by construction.
  * third_party/blink/renderer/core/events/navigator_events.cc - maxTouchPoints.

Requires core/build-gn.patch (the //components/lobium_fp dep on blink core, blink common and
components/embedder_support:user_agent) and core/config-channel.patch (the transport).

